## chopratejas/headroom

Source: https://github.com/chopratejas/headroom
Files:  SRC/neothd/src/context/compress/*.rs

NEOTH's WS-HR token-compression pipeline is a native Rust port of headroom's
`headroom-core` transforms. Per-file provenance (headroom path -> NEOTH file):

| headroom (crates/headroom-core/src/...)        | NEOTH (src/context/compress/...) |
|------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|
| transforms/content_detector.rs                 | content_detector.rs              |
| ccr/ (mod.rs + in_memory backend)              | ccr.rs                           |
| transforms/pipeline/{traits,orchestrator}.rs   | transform.rs + pipeline.rs       |
| transforms/pipeline/reformats/log_template.rs  | log_template.rs                  |
| transforms/log_compressor.rs + log_offload.rs  | log_compressor.rs                |
| transforms/pipeline/offloads/diff_noise.rs     | diff_compressor.rs               |
| transforms/pipeline/reformats/json_minifier.rs | smart_crusher.rs (JsonMinifier)  |
| transforms/smart_crusher/ (sampling)           | smart_crusher.rs (SmartCrusher)  |
| transforms/pipeline/offloads/search_offload.rs | search_compressor.rs             |
| transforms/tag_protector.rs                    | tag_protector.rs                 |

### Modifications (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))

This is a re-implementation with significant changes, all to keep NEOTH
self-contained (no ML, minimal deps):

- The magika ML content detector is OMITTED -- only the heuristic regex path
  is ported.
- CCR keys use SHA-256[:24] (NEOTH already depends on `sha2`) instead of
  headroom's BLAKE3; the in-memory store uses one `std::sync::Mutex<HashMap>`
  instead of a sharded `DashMap`.
- The log offload scores line importance with a small regex heuristic instead
  of headroom's aho-corasick `KeywordDetector`.
- `DiffCompressor` folds headroom's `DiffNoise` together with context-trimming
  and a file cap via a lean line-walker (not the 1600-line unified-diff parser).
- `SmartCrusher` is a head/strided-middle/tail row sampler, not headroom's
  20-module statistical crusher (Kneedle saturation / simhash / outliers).
- `tag_protector` provides a line-level protected-region guard rather than the
  full placeholder-swap (NEOTH's compressors are structural, not ML-text).
- The pipeline runs sequentially (no `rayon`).

